5. Webster's Second International (via /usr/share/dict/words)
--------------------------------------------------------------
The 234,428-word English list embedded at
`crates/mukti-core/data/english-words.fst` is compiled from the word list
shipped with macOS and the BSDs, which is Webster's Second International
(1934). Its copyright has lapsed and it is in the public domain.

Its own README states: "Welcome to web2 (Webster's Second International) all
234,936 words worth. The 1934 copyright has lapsed, according to the supplier."

It is compiled in rather than read from the operating system at runtime,
because Windows has no equivalent file and a guard that silently disappears on
one platform is worse than no guard at all.


6. Rust dependencies
---------------------
Audited at the Phase 7 release gate. 484 packages in the full tree, every one
declaring a licence, all permissive. No GPL, AGPL or SSPL anywhere.

Direct dependencies of the shipped crates:

  fst                 Unlicense OR MIT   the two embedded dictionaries
  quick-xml           MIT                reading and writing Office XML
  zip                 MIT                Office files are ZIP archives
  lopdf               MIT                reading PDFs
  tauri               MIT OR Apache-2.0  the desktop window
  tauri-plugin-dialog MIT OR Apache-2.0  open and save dialogs
  serde               MIT OR Apache-2.0  passing data to the window

Where a package offers a choice of licences, this project takes **MIT**.

Five packages in the tree are **MPL-2.0**, all of them part of the web view
Tauri uses to draw the window:

  cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, option-ext, selectors

MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft. It permits distribution inside a larger MIT
work; the obligation is to publish modifications to the MPL-licensed files
themselves. None of them are modified here. Their source is available from
crates.io and from the Mozilla project.

One package (`r-efi`) offers "MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later". The MIT
option is taken; no LGPL obligation arises.

Full licence texts for every dependency can be regenerated at any time with
`cargo license` or `cargo about`.

7. Fonts — Noto Sans and Noto Sans Bengali
-------------------------------------------
Both bundled with the desktop app, at `crates/mukti-app/ui/fonts/`:

  NotoSans-variable.ttf           1,581,884 bytes
  NotoSansBengali-variable.ttf      372,212 bytes

Source: https://github.com/notofonts/notofonts.github.io
Licence: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1

Verified rather than assumed: each font's own embedded licence field (name
table ID 13) reads "This Font Software is licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1" and points at https://openfontlicense.org.

Worth recording why that check was worth doing. The Noto repository's root
LICENSE file is **Apache-2.0**, which covers the repository's build tooling
and NOT the fonts. It was downloaded first and would have been shipped here as
the fonts' licence — the wrong licence, attached to the wrong thing, in the
one file whose whole job is to get that right.

The OFL requires this text to travel with the fonts. It is reproduced in full
below and kept beside them at `crates/mukti-app/ui/fonts/OFL.txt`.

